cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Computational Digital Twin of Saccharomyces boulardii CNCM I-745"
authors:
  - family-names: Deshmukh
    given-names: Niraj
    email: niraj_20254009@students.iisertirupati.ac.in
    affiliation: "Indian Institute of Science Education and Research Tirupati"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nsdeshmukh306-ai/cncm-i745-digital-twin"
url: "https://github.com/nsdeshmukh306-ai/cncm-i745-digital-twin"
abstract: >
  A five-layer computational digital twin of the probiotic yeast
  Saccharomyces boulardii CNCM I-745, integrating a strain-specific
  genome-scale metabolic model (Yeast9 + GPR corrections), E-Flux
  expression-constrained FBA (Gasch 2000 proxy), ODE-based host-microbe
  pharmacodynamics, and a CNN surrogate model (R2 = 0.8826). Served
  through a FastAPI backend and Streamlit dashboard with a DeepSeek
  natural-language chatbot.
keywords:
  - "Saccharomyces boulardii"
  - "CNCM I-745"
  - "digital twin"
  - "genome-scale metabolic model"
  - "flux balance analysis"
  - "E-Flux"
  - "probiotic"
  - "systems biology"
  - "machine learning surrogate"
  - "host-microbe interaction"
